Subject: [PATCH 08/63] DEMO CODE only adding headers VHAL

Summary:
Fix header for  VHAL proxy server launcher for automotive Android emulation

Implements launcher for Vehicle Hardware Abstraction Layer (VHAL) proxy server
to enable automotive Android features in Cuttlefish. Supports both VHost-User
VSOCK and traditional VSOCK transport with cross-platform compatibility.

Key features:
- Configurable Ethernet endpoint (192.168.98.1:9300+)
- Multi-instance support with incremental ports
- macOS/Linux VSOCK header compatibility
- Conditional startup based on configuration

Enables testing of Android Automotive OS (AAOS) applications without physical
vehicle hardware by bridging VHAL calls between guest and host simulation.

Test Plan:
. build/envsetup.sh
lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz -k &> ~/build.logs.txt
